    [ "$(queue_tier 3)" = 'ready|opus|3|;blocked|opus|1|;ready|opus|Q12, Q13|;blocked|opus|Q14|;ready|opus|Q26|;' ] \
        || fail "tier 3 with the third group not worked out: Q12 and Q26 met a lane and are ready now, Q14 still waits: $(queue_tier 3)"

    sed -i -E 's/  pinned\/[0-9]+ /  /' "$hub/docs/queue.md"
    sed -i '/^Q21  /a Q23  1  todo  opus  docs/n.md  from/Q21 a row filed from Q21 §432' "$hub/docs/queue.md"
    # §450.3 rule 1 (Q2003): three open rows on a_family.rs, one by an item and
    # one in tier 5, and a parked fourth that is no member; three on
    # a_traced_family.rs that a closed trace named, so no family.
    sed -i '/^Q23  /a Q40  1  todo  opus  crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_family.rs  from/- a row on a test file §450\
    Q41  1  todo  opus  crates/rcad-topo/src/fuse/,crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_family.rs#a_test  from/- a second row on it, by an item §450\
    Q43  1  parked:§450  opus  crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_family.rs  from/- a parked row on it, no member §450\
    Q44  1  todo  opus  crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_traced_family.rs  from/- a row a trace named §450\
    Q45  1  todo  opus  crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_traced_family.rs  from/- a second row a trace named §450\
    Q46  1  todo  opus  crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_traced_family.rs  from/- a third row a trace named §450' "$hub/docs/queue.md"
    sed -i '/^Q6  /a Q42  5  todo  opus  crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_family.rs  refuses/C from/- a third row on it, in tier 5 §450' "$hub/docs/queue.md"
    sed -i '/^D1  /a Q47  1  done:abcdef6  opus  -  from/- Trace the family on crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_traced_family.rs: Q44, Q45 and Q46 §450' "$hub/docs/queue.md"
    g add docs/queue.md
    GIT_COMMITTER_DATE='2026-09-05T10:00:00+00:00' g commit -q -m "commit E: every pin taken off, and Q23 filed from Q21"
    sha_e=$(g rev-parse HEAD)
    render || fail "queue-page failed to render with no row pinned"
    [ "$(between 'Pinned' 'Rows the fill will not take now' | grep -c '<p>nothing pinned</p>')" -eq 1 ] \
        || fail "with no row pinned, the pinned table should say nothing is"
    families=$(between 'Families' 'Queue')
    grep -qF '<tr><td class="n">3</td><td><code>crates/rcad-topo/tests/a_family.rs</code></td><td><code><a href="rows/Q40.html">Q40</a></code> (1) <code><a href="rows/Q41.html">Q41</a></code> (1) <code><a href="rows/Q42.html">Q42</a></code> (5)</td></tr>' <<<"$families" \
        || fail "the Families section should hold a_family.rs with its three open rows, each linked with its tier, and not the parked Q43: $families"
    ! grep -qF 'a_traced_family.rs' <<<"$families" || fail "the Families section holds a_traced_family.rs, whose three rows a closed trace named"
    on_page Q23 "<li><code><a href=\"Q23.html\">Q23</a></code>, added in <code>${sha_e:0:8}</code> on 2026-09-05, <q>commit E: every pin taken off, and <a href=\"Q23.html\">Q23</a> filed from <a href=\"Q21.html\">Q21</a></q>: came from <code><a href=\"Q21.html\">Q21</a></code>, as its own word says</li>" \
        "Q23 came from Q21, as its word says, and its commit's subject links the Q ids it names"
    [ "$(chain Q23)" = 'Q23 Q21 Q4 Q3 Q1 ' ] \
        || fail "Q23's page should trace it to Q21, from commit E's summary worked out new, and on through the word still planted in commit D's: $(chain Q23)"

    jq '.shape = -1' "$out/.lineage-cache.json" > "$out/planted.json" && mv "$out/planted.json" "$out/.lineage-cache.json" \
        || fail "could not change the lineage cache's shape"
    render || fail "queue-page failed to render with the lineage cache kept under another shape"
    [ "$(chain Q23)" = 'Q23 Q21 Q2 ' ] \
        || fail "a lineage cache kept under another shape should be worked out again from git, which gives Q21's own word, Q2, not the planted Q4: $(chain Q23)"
    [ "$(results Q2)" = '( Q21 ( Q23 ) ) ' ] || fail "the tree below Q2 should hold Q21, and Q23 below Q21, which commit E filed from it: $(results Q2)"
    echo "check-queue-page-selftest: both charts' counts match a hand count at all four commits, so do the statistics table's first three days, the running table names each held row's tier, agent and dispatcher, the pinned table names what holds each pinned row back in the order of its pin, the table of rows the fill will not take puts each reason beside the rows it holds back, the Families section holds a family and not one a trace named, Pace leads the page, the Queue section counts each tier's ready and blocked rows by model and lists them in runs, every Q id that is a row links to that row's page, which gives its tier, class, write set, text, where it came from and what came from it, the lineage cache serves a kept commit and works out a new one, and the fuzzing section matches its fixture nights"

# Holds `docs/queue.md` to the shape §230.2 gives it, because `queue next`
# dispatches from it and a row it misreads is a lane sent to the wrong place.
#
# **Headings**: the tiers 1, 2, 2.2, 2.5, 3, 4 and 5 and then `## Closed`, each at
# most once and in that order, and no fenced block under anything else, since
# rows there would be rows nobody ranked. `## Closed` must be there; a tier with
# no rows may leave its heading out, and `just queue add` or `tier` writes it
# when a row first goes there (§307.3). **Rows**: a unique id, a real tier, a state from the grammar, a model,
# a write set, and a description whose last word is the section that argues for
# it. An `after:` names rows that can still finish: one naming a dropped row is
# refused with the `just queue after` step that frees the row or keeps its other
# waits (§451). An open row sits under its own tier, and a closed one under
# Closed.
#
# **A class is the first word of a defect's description** (§352.2): wrong,
# crash or refuses, then `/` and a bucket A to D. A first word shaped like a
# class that is none of them is refused as a typo, and so is a class on a row of
# a tier other than 1 and 5, since the fill ranks only those by class. The class
# names an open row's tier (§403): A and B sit in tier 1, C and D in tier 5.
# A tier 5 row with no class is refused unless its `after:` names a tier 5 row,
# open or closed, or a `Q` row this copy does not hold (§435.5); one a lane
# holds, or a parked one, passes, since `take` and `park` write over the
# `after:` that said why it is there. A closed row keeps the tier it closed in.
# `small` has nothing to check: any tier may carry it.
#
# **A row that waits sits in no tier the fill reaches before an open row it
# waits on** (§435): 1, 2, 2.2, 2.5, 3, 4, then 5. The refusal names both rows
# and their tiers. A row with no class and no pin is told to move down; one
# whose class or pin keeps it where it is is left to Mattias (§435.4).
#
# **A pin comes before the class** (§430): `pinned/<n>`, n a number from 1,
# then the class or `small` if the row has one, and the class rules above read
# that second word. An open pinned row is tier 1, and no two open rows share a
# pin. A closed row keeps its pin, so a number may come back once its row has
# closed.
#
# **After the pin and the tag comes the word that says where the row came
# from** (§432): `from/<id>`, `was/<id>` or `from/-`, or `from/fuzz:<target>`
# or `from/step:<file>` for a fault a fuzz target or a corpus file shows
# (§433). Rows filed before §432 have none, so a row without one passes. A
# malformed one is refused, and so are a kind of input other than `fuzz` and
# `step`, a row that says it comes from itself, a T or D id that is not a row,
# and a tag written after the word, where the fill no longer reads it. A `Q` id
# this copy does not hold passes, for the reason the next paragraph gives for
# `after:`. A target or a corpus file is read for its shape only, a kind and
# then a name: one renamed or gone since the row named it passes (§433.4).
#
# **An `after:` may name a `Q` row this copy does not hold yet** (§263.5): the
# other dispatcher's new row, handed out by `just queue add` in its worktree and
# not merged here. A tree cannot see another worktree, so the gate cannot tell
# that row from a typo; `just queue after` can, and refuses an id that exists
# nowhere. A `T` or `D` id is never handed out again, so one missing is refused.
#
# **Write sets are held against what git tracks, not against the disk.**
# `fuzz/artifacts/` is here and not on a fresh clone, so `[ -e ]` would pass
# here and fail on the runner, which is §173's kind of check. A path passes when
# git tracks it or the directory it would go in, because a lane may create the
# file. A tracked directory written without its `/` is refused: it would meet
# nothing under it. Closed rows are held to the grammar only, since a file a
# merged row wrote may have moved since.
#
# **A `done:` sha and a `lane:` branch are held to their shape only.** CI's
# checkout is shallow and `gate-fresh` clones one branch, so neither the commit
# nor the lane branch has to exist where this runs (§77.6).
#
# Citations are checked against the concatenation of `docs/decisions.d`, the way
# `check-where-the-work-is` reads it (§179). A file with no rows fails, because
# it would pass having checked nothing.
[doc("docs/queue.md is shaped as §230.2 and §307 say, and every section its rows cite exists.")]
check-queue file=queue_file:
    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    set -uo pipefail
    all=$(mktemp)
    trap 'rm -f "$all"' EXIT
    here=(--justfile '{{ justfile() }}' --working-directory "$PWD")
    {{ just_executable() }} "${here[@]}" decisions-all > "$all" || exit 1
    {{ just_executable() }} "${here[@]}" _queue-check '{{ file }}' "$all"

[doc("Check a queue file against §230.2, citing sections from the given decisions file.")]
_queue-check file decisions:
    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    set -uo pipefail
    rows=$({{ just_executable() }} --justfile '{{ justfile() }}' --working-directory "$PWD" _queue-rows '{{ file }}') || exit 1
    tracked=$(git ls-files) || exit 1
    [ -f '{{ decisions }}' ] || { echo "_queue-check: {{ decisions }} is not a file" >&2; exit 1; }
    {
        printf '%s\n' "$tracked" | awk '{ print "P\037" $0 }'
        awk '/^## [0-9]+\. / || /^### [0-9]+\.[0-9]+ / { print "S\037" $2 }' '{{ decisions }}'
        printf '%s\n' "$rows"
    } | LC_ALL=C awk -v file='{{ file }}' -v slots='{{ queue_slots }}' '
        BEGIN {
            FS = "\037"
            nt = split("1 2 2.2 2.5 3 4 5", tiers, " ")
            for (i = 1; i <= nt; i++) {
                rank[tiers[i]] = i; istier[tiers[i]] = 1
                headings = headings "Tier " tiers[i] ", "
                named = named (i == 1 ? "" : i == nt ? " or " : ", ") tiers[i]
            }
            rank["closed"] = nt + 1
            headings = headings "Closed"
        }
        $1 == "P" {
            tracked[$2] = 1
            p = $2
            while (match(p, /\/[^\/]*$/)) { p = substr(p, 1, RSTART); tracked[p] = 1; p = substr(p, 1, RSTART - 1) }
            next
        }
        $1 == "S" { s = $2; sub(/\.$/, "", s); sec[s] = 1; next }
        $1 == "H" {
            k = key($3)
            if (k == "") next
            if (k in seen) err($2, "heading \"## " $3 "\" appears twice; the first is on line " seen[k])
            else {
                if (rank[k] < last) err($2, "heading \"## " $3 "\" is out of order; they go " headings)
                seen[k] = $2
            }
            if (rank[k] > last) last = rank[k]
            next
        }
        $1 == "F" && $3 == "open" && key($4) == "" {
            err($2, "a fenced block under " ($4 == "" ? "no heading" : "\"## " $4 "\"") ", and only the " nt " tiers and Closed may hold one")
            next
        }
        $1 == "U" { err($2, "this fence is never closed, so every line after it reads as a row"); next }
        $1 == "R" {
            line = $2; head = $3; id = $5; tier = $6; state = $7; model = $8; ws = $9; what = $10
            rows++
            if ($4 < 6) { err(line, id ": a row is five fields and a description, and this one has " $4 " fields"); next }
            if (id !~ /^[TDQ][0-9]+$/) err(line, id ": an id is T, D or Q and then a number")
            if (id in at) err(line, id ": the id is used on line " at[id] " too")
            else at[id] = line
            if (!(tier in istier)) err(line, id ": tier \"" tier "\" is not " named)
            kind = ""
            if (state == "todo") kind = "todo"
            else if (state ~ /^lane:[A-Za-z0-9._\/-]+$/) kind = "lane"
            else if (state ~ /^after:[TDQ][0-9]+(,[TDQ][0-9]+)*$/) kind = "after"
            else if (state ~ /^done:[0-9a-f]+$/ && length(state) >= 12 && length(state) <= 45) kind = "done"
            else if (state ~ /^dropped:§[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$/) kind = "dropped"
            else if (state ~ /^parked:§[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$/) kind = "parked"
            else err(line, id ": state \"" state "\" is not todo, lane:<branch>, after:<id>[,<id>], done:<sha>, dropped:§N or parked:§N")
            kindof[id] = kind
            closed = (kind == "done" || kind == "dropped")
            if (kind == "dropped" || kind == "parked") cite(line, id, substr(state, index(state, ":") + 1))
            if (kind == "after") { wid[++nw] = id; waits[id] = substr(state, 7); wline[id] = line }
            if (kind == "todo") ready++
            if (kind == "lane") running++
            if (kind == "parked") parked++
            if (closed) closedrows++
            if (model == "-") {
                if (!closed) err(line, id ": model \"-\" is for a closed row that never recorded one, and this row is open")
            } else if (model != "opus" && model != "sonnet") err(line, id ": model \"" model "\" is not opus or sonnet")
            if (ws != "-") {
                m = split(ws, e, ",")
                for (i = 1; i <= m; i++) entry(line, id, e[i], closed)
            }
            n = split(what, w, " ")
            if (n == 0 || w[n] !~ /^§[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$/) err(line, id ": the description does not end in a §N or §N.M")
            pinned = (w[1] ~ /^pinned\//)
            if (pinned && w[1] !~ /^pinned\/[1-9][0-9]*$/) err(line, id ": \"" w[1] "\" is not a pin: pinned/ and then a number from 1 (§430)")
            else if (pinned && !closed) {
                if (tier != "1") err(line, id ": an open pinned row is tier 1 (§430), and this row is tier " tier)
                if (w[1] in pinline) err(line, id ": " w[1] " is on line " pinline[w[1]] " too, and two open rows never share a pin")
                else pinline[w[1]] = line
            }
            tag = pinned ? w[2] : w[1]
            isclass = (tag ~ /^(wrong|crash|refuses)\/[ABCD]$/)
            if (tag ~ /^[a-z]+\/[A-Z]$/ && !isclass) err(line, id ": \"" tag "\" is not a class: wrong, crash or refuses, then /A, /B, /C or /D")
            else if (isclass && tier != "1" && tier != "5") err(line, id ": the class " tag " ranks tier 1 and tier 5 rows only, and this row is tier " tier)
            else if (isclass && !closed) {
                want = (tag ~ /\/[CD]$/) ? "5" : "1"
                if (tier != want) err(line, id ": the class " tag " puts an open row in tier " want ", and this row is tier " tier "; move it with just queue tier " id " " want " (§403)")
            }
            tierof[id] = tier
            keeps[id] = (pinned && !closed) ? "pin " w[1] : isclass ? "class " tag : ""
            if (tier == "5" && (kind == "todo" || kind == "after") && !isclass) { five[++n5] = id; fiveline[id] = line }
            fpos = (pinned ? 2 : 1) + ((isclass || tag == "small") ? 1 : 0)
            if (w[fpos] ~ /^(from|was)\//) {
                if (w[fpos] !~ /^(from\/([TDQ][0-9]+|-|(fuzz|step):[^ ]+)|was\/[TDQ][0-9]+)$/) err(line, id ": \"" w[fpos] "\" is not where a row came from: from/<id>, was/<id>, from/-, from/fuzz:<target> or from/step:<file> (§432, §433)")
                else if (w[fpos] ~ /^(from|was)\/[TDQ][0-9]+$/) { fromid[++nfrom] = id; fromsrc[id] = substr(w[fpos], index(w[fpos], "/") + 1); fromline[id] = line }
                if (w[fpos + 1] ~ /^(wrong|crash|refuses)\/[ABCD]$/ || w[fpos + 1] == "small") err(line, id ": the tag " w[fpos + 1] " goes before " w[fpos] ", where the fill reads it (§432)")
            }
            s = what
            while (match(s, /§[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?/)) { cite(line, id, substr(s, RSTART, RLENGTH)); s = substr(s, RSTART + RLENGTH) }
            hk = key(head)
            if (hk != "" && kind != "") {
                if (closed && hk != "closed") err(line, id ": a " kind " row sits under \"## " head "\", and closed rows go under ## Closed")
                else if (!closed && hk != tier && (tier in istier)) err(line, id ": a tier " tier " row sits under \"## " head "\"")
            }
            next
        }
        END {
            for (i = 1; i <= nw; i++) {
                id = wid[i]; ok = 1
                m = split(waits[id], a, ",")
                rest = ""
                for (j = 1; j <= m; j++) if (!((a[j] in kindof) && kindof[a[j]] == "dropped")) rest = rest (rest == "" ? "" : ",") a[j]
                for (j = 1; j <= m; j++) {
                    if (a[j] == id) err(wline[id], id ": waits on itself")
                    else if (!(a[j] in kindof) && a[j] ~ /^Q/) notheld++
                    else if (!(a[j] in kindof)) err(wline[id], id ": waits on " a[j] ", which is not a row in this file, and a T or D id is never handed out again")
                    else if (kindof[a[j]] == "dropped") err(wline[id], id ": waits on " a[j] ", which was dropped and will never be done; " (rest == "" ? "just queue after " id " - frees it, and just queue after " id " <id> makes it wait on a row that replaces " a[j] : "just queue after " id " " rest " keeps its other waits, with any row that replaces " a[j] " added to them"))
                    if (kindof[a[j]] != "done") ok = 0
                }
                if (ok) ready++
                else waiting++
            }
            for (i = 1; i <= nw; i++) {
                id = wid[i]
                if (!(tierof[id] in istier)) continue
                m = split(waits[id], a, ",")
                for (j = 1; j <= m; j++) {
                    b = a[j]
                    if (!(b in at) || kindof[b] == "done" || kindof[b] == "dropped" || !(tierof[b] in istier)) continue
                    if (rank[tierof[id]] >= rank[tierof[b]]) continue
                    if (keeps[id] == "") err(wline[id], id ": waits on " b ", which is tier " tierof[b] ", and sits in tier " tierof[id] ", which the fill reaches first; move it down with just queue tier " id " " tierof[b] " (§435)")
                    else err(wline[id], id ": waits on " b ", which is tier " tierof[b] ", and its " keeps[id] " keeps it in tier " tierof[id] ", which the fill reaches first: which of the two moves is Mattias\047s to set (§435.4)")
                }
            }
            for (i = 1; i <= n5; i++) {
                id = five[i]; ok = 0
                if (kindof[id] == "after") {
                    m = split(waits[id], a, ",")
                    for (j = 1; j <= m; j++) if ((a[j] in at) ? tierof[a[j]] == "5" : a[j] ~ /^Q/) ok = 1
                }
                if (!ok) err(fiveline[id], id ": an open tier 5 row carries a class C or D (§403), or waits on a tier 5 row (§435.5), and this one does neither; give it a class with just queue tag, or move it with just queue tier")
            }
            for (i = 1; i <= nfrom; i++) {
                id = fromid[i]; src = fromsrc[id]
                if (src == id) err(fromline[id], id ": says it comes from itself")
                else if (!(src in kindof) && src !~ /^Q/) err(fromline[id], id ": comes from " src ", which is not a row in this file, and a T or D id is never handed out again")
            }
            if (!("closed" in seen)) err("", "heading \"## Closed\" is missing")
            if (rows == 0) err("", "has no rows, so there was nothing to check")
            if (bad) { printf "%s: %d problem%s\n", file, bad, (bad == 1 ? "" : "s"); exit 1 }
            printf "%s: %d rows; %d ready, %d waiting, %d running in %d slots, %d parked, %d closed%s\n", file, rows, ready, waiting, running, slots, parked, closedrows, (notheld ? "; " notheld " wait on a Q row this copy does not hold yet" : "")
        }
        function err(line, msg) {
            if (line == "") printf "%s: %s\n", file, msg
            else printf "%s:%s: %s\n", file, line, msg
            bad++
        }
        function key(h,    w) {
            if (h ~ /^Tier (1|2|2\.2|2\.5|3|4|5)( |$)/) { split(h, w, " "); return w[2] }
            if (h ~ /^Closed( |$)/) return "closed"
            return ""
        }
        function cite(line, id, c) {
            if (!(substr(c, 3) in sec)) err(line, id ": cites " c ", and docs/decisions.d has no such section")
        }
        function entry(line, id, x, closed,    p, h) {
            if (x == "-") { err(line, id ": \"-\" stands alone in a write set, and here it has company"); return }
            if (x !~ /^[A-Za-z0-9._\/-]+(#[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)?$/ || x ~ /^\// || x ~ /\/\//) {
                err(line, id ": \"" x "\" is not a path, a directory ending in /, or path#item")
                return
            }
            p = x; h = index(x, "#")
            if (h) {
                p = substr(x, 1, h - 1)
                if (p !~ /\.rs$/ && p != "justfile") err(line, id ": \"" x "\" names an item, and only a .rs file or the justfile has items")
            }
            if (closed) return
            if (p !~ /\/$/ && ((p "/") in tracked)) err(line, id ": \"" p "\" is a directory; write it as " p "/ so it meets the files under it")
            else if (!(p in tracked) && parent(p) != "" && !(parent(p) in tracked)) err(line, id ": \"" p "\" is not tracked, and neither is the directory it would go in")
        }
        function parent(p) {
            sub(/\/$/, "", p)
            return match(p, /\/[^\/]*$/) ? substr(p, 1, RSTART) : ""
        }
    '

# Pins `check-queue` and `queue` against fixtures, because the live file is
# sound by construction and would pass a check that had stopped checking.
#
# The shape half is one good file, then one copy of it per defect `check-queue`
# names, and one copy with an empty tier's heading left out, which passes
# (§307.3). The fill half is §230.3 case by case: tier order against the order in
# the file, tier 2.2 included, a row a running lane blocks, two items of one fuse
# file taken together while the same item twice is not, a directory blocking a
# file in both directions, `-` fitting beside anything, `after:` on a running row
# and on a done one, and a tier the fill does not know refused. §403 adds tier 5
# taken last though written first, a class naming the wrong tier for an open
# row refused while a closed row keeps its tier, and a tier 5 row with no class
# that waits on nothing refused. §352 adds tiers 1 and 5 in class order against the order in the file,
# with the measure line counted by hand; a full bundle of small rows going ahead
# of tier 1, and a lone small row
# still printed as a bundle; a partial bundle waiting for its tier and pulling the
# later small rows forward, one overlapping its leader; and a small row a running
# lane blocks, which neither joins nor completes a bundle. `blocked` prints the
# skip line of each ready row a running lane holds back, in the fill's order, and
# none for a row only a row taken above holds back, nor for a waiting or a parked
# row (Q1510). §430 adds pinned rows taken first, by number and not by line,
# ahead of a full bundle and of wrong/A; a pinned row a running lane blocks,
# skipped; a class after a pin, still read by the check and the measure; and a
# pin of 0, a pin on a tier 2 row and two open rows on one pin refused, while a
# closed row may keep the pin an open row has. §430.7 adds a pinned row a
# running lane holds back keeping each row the fill reaches after it out of its
# write set, skipped with the pinned row named: a later pin, a wrong/A row, a
# small row that would complete the full bundle, and a third holder of a shared
# file the pin names; a second holder of that file and the rows that meet no pin
# are taken, and `blocked` still names the running lane alone. §432 adds the
# word that says where a row came from, after a pin and a class, after `small`, and on a closed
# row; a `from/` naming a Q row this copy does not hold, passed; and a malformed
# word, `was/-`, a row from itself, a T id that is no row and a class written
# after the word, refused. `add` refuses a row without the word, one naming a
# row that exists nowhere, and `was/-`; writes the word after the tag whichever
# came first; and still refuses a class with punctuation or a pin behind it.
# §433 adds `from/fuzz:<target>` and `from/step:<file>`: on an open row after a
# pin and a class, and on a closed row after `small`, passed by their shape
# alone, a name ending like a row id included; and a kind it does not know, a kind with no name, `was/` with a kind,
# and a class written after the word, refused. `add` takes a target that is
# there, a corpus file by its own name, and one NIST name by its directory
# with the space written `_`, the colon tripping no refusal of a class; and
# refuses a target that is not there, an unknown kind, a name two paths end in,
# a name cut inside a file name, a name longer than it needs, `was/fuzz:`, and
# a class with punctuation behind the word. §435 adds a row in a tier the fill
# reaches before an open row it waits on, refused: with no class and told to
# move down, and with a pin or a class left to Mattias; and a tier 5 row with
# no class that waits on a tier 1 row, refused. A tier 5 row with no class
# passes when it waits on an open tier 5 row, a closed one, or a Q row this
# copy does not hold, and when a lane holds it or it is parked; a row waiting on
# a row in an earlier tier, or on a done row in a later one, passes too. The
# classes fixture's measure line counts its tier 5 row with no class. §424.7
# adds `narrow`, on a claims file of its own: a directory narrowed to a file
# under it, written to the claims file and read back by `running`; an id
# nobody holds, an entry outside the set the row was taken with and a
# directory written without its `/`, refused; and a widening back refused
# while another hold meets the entry it widens to, and passed when none does.
[private]
[doc("check-queue and queue agree with their fixtures: every defect refused, every fill in §230.3's order.")]
check-queue-selftest:
    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    set -uo pipefail
    dir=$(mktemp -d)
    trap 'rm -rf "$dir"' EXIT
    # `queue next` now runs `_triage-refusal`, which reads `RCAD_FUZZ_LOGS`
    # (§418.2); point it at a scratch directory before any `drive`/`bundled`
    # call below runs `queue next`, or every one of them would read this
    # machine's own fuzz logs. `take` and `add` run `queue-page` afterward too
    # (§397.8), so its page dir is pointed at scratch here as well.
    export RCAD_QUEUE_PAGE_DIR="$dir/queue-page"
    export RCAD_FUZZ_LOGS="$dir/no-fuzz-logs"
    j='{{ just_executable() }}'
    got=""
    fail() {
        echo "the queue drifted from its own fixtures: $1"
        echo "--- got ---"; echo "$got"
        exit 1
    }

    # `_queue-check` asks git which paths are tracked, and `check-queue` reads
    # `decisions_dir` from where it runs. Both run in a scratch repository, so
    # this step's answer never rests on what the real tree holds under docs/,
    # which is what lets it be served (§369).
    repo="$dir/repo"
    mkdir -p "$repo/docs/decisions.d" "$repo/.github/workflows" "$repo/tooling/queue"
    decisions="$repo/docs/decisions.d/sections.md"
    printf '%s\n' '## 13. How work is decomposed' '## 226. The test plan' \
        '### 226.3 The nights' '## 230. One queue' '### 230.3 The fill' \
        '## 418. Fuzz-night triage' '### 418.3 The triage row' > "$decisions"
    touch "$repo/justfile" "$repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml" "$repo/tooling/queue/queue.py"
    git init -q "$repo"
    git -C "$repo" add -A
    q() { "$j" --justfile '{{ justfile() }}' --working-directory "$repo" "$@"; }

    cat > "$dir/good.md" <<'MD'
    # A queue

    ## Tier 1 — what a fuse gets wrong

    ```
    T1  1  todo  opus  justfile#queue  pinned/1 refuses/B make the queue fill from the top §230.3
    Q2  1  lane:lane-q2  opus  .github/workflows/ci.yml  a row a lane holds §230
    Q8  1  todo  opus  -  pinned/2 wrong/A from/T9 a defect the first row found §230
    ```

    ## Tier 2

    ```
    Q3  2  after:T9  sonnet  docs/new.md  small waits on a done row, so it is ready §226.3
    ```

    ## Tier 2.2

    ```
    Q6  2.2  todo  sonnet  tooling/queue/  changes how the work is done §230
    Q9  2.2  todo  sonnet  -  was/D1 the dropped row filed again §230
    ```

    ## Tier 2.5

    ```
    Q4  2.5  parked:§13  opus  docs/  parked for want of a consumer §13
    ```

    ## Tier 3

    ```
    Q5  3  after:Q2  sonnet  -  waits on a running lane §230
    ```

    ## Tier 4

    ```
    ```

    ## Tier 5

    ```
    Q7  5  todo  opus  tooling/queue/queue.py  wrong/C a defect only a probe builds §230
    ```

    ## Closed

    ```
    T9  1  done:42df376e  -  justfile  the first row of the test plan §226
    D1  2  dropped:§226  opus  -  dropped for the queue §226
    D2  1  dropped:§226  opus  -  refuses/C closed in tier 1, before tier 5 was there §226
    D3  1  done:42df376e  -  -  pinned/1 closed with its pin, the number T1 has now §230
    D4  2  dropped:§230  opus  -  small from/- a row no other row led to, dropped §230
    ```
    MD

    got=$(q _queue-check "$dir/good.md" "$decisions" 2>&1) \
        || fail "a queue with nothing wrong in it was rejected"
    grep -qF '14 rows; 6 ready, 1 waiting, 1 running in 4 slots, 1 parked, 5 closed' <<<"$got" \
        || fail "the line a pass prints does not count the good queue's rows"
    got=$(q check-queue "$dir/good.md" 2>&1) \
        || fail "check-queue rejected the good queue against the sections in decisions_dir"
    sed '/^## Tier 4$/,+4d' "$dir/good.md" > "$dir/no-tier-4.md"
    grep -q '^## Tier 4' "$dir/no-tier-4.md" && fail "the fixture without Tier 4 still has its heading"
    got=$(q _queue-check "$dir/no-tier-4.md" "$decisions" 2>&1) \
        || fail "a tier with no rows was refused for leaving its heading out"
    sed 's/from\/T9 a defect/from\/Q999 a defect/' "$dir/good.md" > "$dir/from-not-held.md"
    got=$(q _queue-check "$dir/from-not-held.md" "$decisions" 2>&1) \
        || fail "a row that comes from a Q row this copy does not hold yet was refused"
    # §433.4: check-queue reads only the shape of a fuzz target's or a corpus
    # file's name, so a row naming one since renamed or gone still passes.
    sed 's/from\/T9 a defect/from\/fuzz:a_target_since_renamed a defect/' "$dir/good.md" > "$dir/from-fuzz.md"
    grep -qF 'wrong/A from/fuzz:a_target_since_renamed a defect' "$dir/from-fuzz.md" || fail "the from/fuzz: fixture did not change Q8"
    got=$(q _queue-check "$dir/from-fuzz.md" "$decisions" 2>&1) \
        || fail "a pinned row with a class that comes from a fuzz target was refused, though check-queue reads only the shape"
    sed 's/small from\/- a row/small from\/step:CTC_Definitions\/a_file_gone_from_the_corpus.stp a row/' "$dir/good.md" > "$dir/from-step.md"
    grep -qF 'small from/step:CTC_Definitions/a_file_gone_from_the_corpus.stp a row' "$dir/from-step.md" || fail "the from/step: fixture did not change D4"
    got=$(q _queue-check "$dir/from-step.md" "$decisions" 2>&1) \
        || fail "a closed small row that comes from a corpus file was refused, though check-queue reads only the shape"
    sed 's/from\/T9 a defect/from\/step:a_directory\/T99 a defect/' "$dir/good.md" > "$dir/from-step-like-a-row.md"
    grep -qF 'wrong/A from/step:a_directory/T99 a defect' "$dir/from-step-like-a-row.md" || fail "the from/step: fixture ending like a row id did not change Q8"
    got=$(q _queue-check "$dir/from-step-like-a-row.md" "$decisions" 2>&1) \
        || fail "a corpus name ending in /T99 was read as the row T99"

    refused() {
        sed "$2" "$dir/good.md" > "$dir/$1.md"
        got=$(q _queue-check "$dir/$1.md" "$decisions" 2>&1) \
            && fail "$1: a queue with this defect was accepted"
        grep -qF -- "$3" <<<"$got" || fail "$1: the refusal does not say '$3'"
    }
    refused twice       's/^## Tier 3$/## Tier 2/'                  'appears twice'
    refused order       's/^## Tier 1 .*/## Tier 2.5/'              'out of order'
    refused missing     '/^## Closed$/d'                            '"## Closed" is missing'
    refused stray       's/^## Tier 4$/## Notes/'                   'under "## Notes"'
    refused unclosed    '$d'                                        'never closed'
    refused id          's/^Q4 /X4 /'                               'X4: an id is'
    grep -qE "^$dir/id.md:[0-9]+: X4: " <<<"$got" || fail "id: the refusal does not name the line and the id"
    refused same-id     's/^Q5 /Q4 /'                               'the id is used on line'
    refused tier        's/^T1  1 /T1  7 /'                         'tier "7"'
    refused state       's/lane:lane-q2/running/'                   'state "running"'
    refused sha         's/done:42df376e/done:42DF/'                'state "done:42DF"'
    refused after-none  's/after:Q2/after:T99/'                     'T99, which is not a row'
    refused after-self  's/after:Q2/after:Q5/'                      'waits on itself'
    refused after-drop  's/after:Q2/after:D1/'                      'Q5: waits on D1, which was dropped and will never be done; just queue after Q5 - frees it, and just queue after Q5 <id> makes it wait on a row that replaces D1'
    refused after-drop-rest 's/after:Q2/after:D1,Q2/'               'Q5: waits on D1, which was dropped and will never be done; just queue after Q5 Q2 keeps its other waits, with any row that replaces D1 added to them'
    refused model       's/^T1  1  todo  opus/T1  1  todo  haiku/'  'model "haiku"'
    refused open-dash   's/^T1  1  todo  opus/T1  1  todo  -/'      'model "-"'
    refused dash-beside 's/  -  waits/  -,docs\/  waits/'           'stands alone'
    refused untracked   's/docs\/new.md/nowhere\/new.md/'           '"nowhere/new.md" is not tracked'
    refused bare-dir    's/  docs\/  parked/  docs  parked/'        'write it as docs/'
    refused item        's/workflows\/ci.yml/workflows\/ci.yml#job/' 'only a .rs file or the justfile'
    refused last-token  's/ §230.3$/ §230.3 later/'                 'does not end in'
    refused no-section  's/ §226.3$/ §226.9/'                       'cites §226.9'
    refused no-parked   's/parked:§13/parked:§14/'                  'cites §14'
    refused placed      's/^Q3  2 /Q3  3 /'                         'a tier 3 row sits under'
    refused placed-2.2  's/^Q6  2.2 /Q6  2 /'                       'a tier 2 row sits under "## Tier 2.2"'
    refused order-2.2   's/^## Tier 2$/X/; s/^## Tier 2.2$/## Tier 2/; s/^X$/## Tier 2.2/' '"## Tier 2" is out of order'
    refused closed-open 's/^Q4  2.5  parked:§13/Q4  2.5  done:abcdef0/' 'a done row sits under'
    refused fields      's/^Q4 .*/Q4  2.5  parked:§13  opus  docs\//' 'five fields and a description'
    refused empty       '/^[TDQ][0-9]/d'                            'has no rows'
    refused class-typo  's/refuses\/B make/wrong\/E make/'          '"wrong/E" is not a class'
    refused class-tier  's/  changes how the work/  wrong\/C changes how the work/' 'the class wrong/C ranks tier 1 and tier 5 rows only, and this row is tier 2.2'
    refused c-in-tier-1 's/refuses\/B make/refuses\/C make/'        'the class refuses/C puts an open row in tier 5, and this row is tier 1'
    refused b-in-tier-5 's/wrong\/C a defect/wrong\/B a defect/'    'the class wrong/B puts an open row in tier 1, and this row is tier 5'
    refused no-class-5  's/  wrong\/C a defect/  a defect/'         'an open tier 5 row carries a class C or D'
    refused pin-zero    's/pinned\/1 refuses/pinned\/0 refuses/'   '"pinned/0" is not a pin'
    refused pin-tier-2  's/  small waits on a done row/  pinned\/2 small waits on a done row/' 'an open pinned row is tier 1 (§430), and this row is tier 2'
    refused pin-twice   's/  a row a lane holds/  pinned\/1 a row a lane holds/' 'pinned/1 is on line'
    refused from-shape  's/was\/D1 the/was\/X1 the/'                '"was/X1" is not where a row came from'
    refused was-nothing 's/was\/D1 the/was\/- the/'                 '"was/-" is not where a row came from'
    refused from-self   's/was\/D1 the/was\/Q9 the/'                'Q9: says it comes from itself'
    refused from-none   's/from\/T9 a defect/from\/T99 a defect/'   'comes from T99, which is not a row'
    refused from-first  's/wrong\/A from\/T9/from\/T9 wrong\/A/'    'the tag wrong/A goes before from/T9'
    refused from-kind   's/from\/T9 a defect/from\/night:10-11 a defect/' '"from/night:10-11" is not where a row came from'
    refused fuzz-empty  's/from\/T9 a defect/from\/fuzz: a defect/'  '"from/fuzz:" is not where a row came from'
    refused step-empty  's/from\/T9 a defect/from\/step: a defect/'  '"from/step:" is not where a row came from'
    refused was-input   's/was\/D1 the/was\/fuzz:where_two_surfaces_cross the/' '"was/fuzz:where_two_surfaces_cross" is not where a row came from'
    refused fuzz-first  's/wrong\/A from\/T9/from\/fuzz:where_two_surfaces_cross wrong\/A/' 'the tag wrong/A goes before from/fuzz:where_two_surfaces_cross'
    refused waits-above 's/after:Q2/after:Q7/'                      'Q5: waits on Q7, which is tier 5, and sits in tier 3, which the fill reaches first; move it down with just queue tier Q5 5 (§435)'
    refused pin-above   's/^T1  1  todo /T1  1  after:Q7 /'         "T1: waits on Q7, which is tier 5, and its pin pinned/1 keeps it in tier 1, which the fill reaches first: which of the two moves is Mattias's to set (§435.4)"
    refused class-above 's/^T1  1  todo  opus  justfile#queue  pinned\/1 /T1  1  after:Q7  opus  justfile#queue  /' "T1: waits on Q7, which is tier 5, and its class refuses/B keeps it in tier 1, which the fill reaches first: which of the two moves is Mattias's to set (§435.4)"
    refused five-on-one 's/^Q7  5  todo  opus  tooling\/queue\/queue.py  wrong\/C a defect/Q7  5  after:Q8  opus  tooling\/queue\/queue.py  a defect/' 'Q7: an open tier 5 row carries a class C or D (§403), or waits on a tier 5 row (§435.5), and this one does neither'

    passes() {
        sed "$2" "$dir/good.md" > "$dir/$1.md"
        cmp -s "$dir/good.md" "$dir/$1.md" && fail "$1: the fixture did not change the good queue"
        got=$(q _queue-check "$dir/$1.md" "$decisions" 2>&1) || fail "$1: $3"
    }
    nofive='s/^Q7  5  todo  opus  tooling\/queue\/queue.py  wrong\/C a defect/Q7  5  STATE  opus  tooling\/queue\/queue.py  a defect/'
    passes five-on-open   "/^Q7 /a Q10  5  after:Q7  sonnet  -  no class, waiting on a tier 5 defect §230" \
        'a tier 5 row with no class that waits on an open tier 5 row was refused'
    passes five-on-closed "${nofive/STATE/after:D5}; /^D4 /a D5  5  done:42df376e  opus  -  wrong/C a defect closed in tier 5 §230" \
        'a tier 5 row with no class that waits on a closed tier 5 row was refused'
    passes five-on-unheld "${nofive/STATE/after:Q999}" \
        'a tier 5 row with no class that waits on a Q row this copy does not hold was refused'
    passes five-held      "${nofive/STATE/lane:lane-q7}" \
        'a tier 5 row with no class that a lane holds was refused, though take writes over its after:'
    passes five-parked    "${nofive/STATE/parked:§230}" \
        'a parked tier 5 row with no class was refused, though park writes over its after:'
    passes waits-below    's/^Q3  2  after:T9 /Q3  2  after:Q8 /' \
        'a tier 2 row that waits on a tier 1 row was refused'
    passes waits-on-done  "s/^Q3  2  after:T9 /Q3  2  after:D5 /; /^D4 /a D5  5  done:42df376e  opus  -  wrong/C a defect closed in tier 5 §230" \
        'a tier 2 row that waits on a done tier 5 row was refused, though the fill reaches it as soon as it is ready'

    fence() { { echo '```'; cat; echo '```'; } > "$dir/$1.md"; }
    drive() {
        got=$("$j" --set queue_file "$dir/$1.md" --set queue_running 1 queue "${@:2}" 2>&1) \
            || fail "queue ${*:2} failed on the $1 fixture"
    }
    takes() { grep '^take ' <<<"$got" | cut -d' ' -f2 | tr '\n' ' '; }

    fence order <<'MD'
    Q50  5  todo  opus  docs/g.md  wrong/C tier five, written first §230
    Q30  3  todo  opus  docs/a.md  tier three §230
    Q25  2.5  todo  opus  docs/b.md  tier two and a half §230
    Q22  2.2  todo  opus  docs/f.md  tier two point two, written above tier two §230
    Q20  2  todo  opus  docs/c.md  tier two §230
    T11  1  todo  opus  docs/d.md  tier one §230
    T12  1  todo  opus  docs/e.md  tier one again §230
    Q40  4  todo  opus  docs/h.md  tier four §230
    MD
    drive order next 2
    [ "$(takes)" = "T11 T12 " ] || fail "two slots did not go to the two tier 1 rows"
    grep -qx 'took 2 of 2' <<<"$got" || fail "a full fill did not say it took all it was asked for"
    drive order next 4
    [ "$(takes)" = "T11 T12 Q20 Q22 " ] \
        || fail "tier 2.2 was not taken after tier 2, which is written below it in the file"
    drive order next 5
    [ "$(takes)" = "T11 T12 Q20 Q22 Q25 " ] \
        || fail "tier 2.5 was not taken after tier 2.2, and before tier 3, which is written above both"
    drive order next 8
    [ "$(takes)" = "T11 T12 Q20 Q22 Q25 Q30 Q40 Q50 " ] \
        || fail "tier 5 was not taken last, after tier 4, though it is written first"

    fence classes <<'MD'
    Q1  1  todo  opus  docs/a.md  no class, written first §230
    Q2  5  todo  opus  docs/b.md  refuses/D a refusal only past the scale envelope §230
    Q3  1  todo  opus  docs/c.md  refuses/A a refusal a real file met §230
    Q4  5  todo  opus  docs/d.md  crash/C a crash only a probe builds §230
    Q5  1  todo  opus  docs/e.md  wrong/B a wrong answer on a flush pair §230
    Q6  5  todo  opus  docs/f.md  wrong/D a wrong answer at 1e308 §230
    Q7  1  todo  opus  docs/g.md  wrong/B another wrong answer, later in the file §230
    Q8  2  todo  opus  docs/h.md  tier two §230
    Q9  1  parked:§230  opus  docs/i.md  wrong/A parked, so out of the measure §230
    Q10  5  todo  opus  docs/j.md  refuses/C a refusal only a probe builds §230
    Q11  4  todo  opus  docs/k.md  tier four §230
    Q12  5  after:Q13  opus  docs/l.md  no class, ready in tier 5 since the row it waits on is done §230
    Q13  5  done:42df376e  opus  docs/m.md  wrong/C closed, and Q12 waited on it §230
    MD
    drive classes next 11
    [ "$(takes)" = "Q5 Q7 Q3 Q1 Q8 Q11 Q4 Q10 Q12 Q6 Q2 " ] \
        || fail "tiers 1 and 5 were not each taken wrong before crash before refuses, A before B and C before D, with no class after B and between C and D"
    drive classes
    grep -qxF 'tier 1, open and not parked: 3 in A or B (2 wrong, 0 crash, 1 refuses), 1 with no class; tier 5: 2 in C, 2 in D, 1 with no class; 0 small rows ready, and a bundle is 5' <<<"$got" \
        || fail "the measure line does not count the classes fixture's tier 1 and tier 5 rows, the tier 5 row with no class among them"

    # §450.3 rule 1 (Q2003): the rows on two_equal_bars_leaning_at_each_other.rs,
    # copied as 16eab121's docs/queue.md held them, are the family Q1953 traced.
    # A closed row and a parked one on the file are no members, and Q1991 names
    # one file twice, by two items, and counts once. A trace, open or closed,
    # takes out the rows it names; the file is a family again with three rows no
    # trace names, and a row a trace on another file named counts on a file no
    # trace has been on.
    fence families <<'MD'
    Q1793 1    after:Q1660    opus    crates/rcad-topo/src/fuse/,crates/rcad-topo/tests/two_equal_bars_leaning_at_each_other.rs   refuses/B was/Q1656 Two bars of radius 1/4 through (11,0,0), the second 32 long turned 120 degrees about z, stored direction (-0.5,0.866,-2.2e-16) (a_long_bar_through_another_at_120_degrees_is_refused_meshing_or_building_a_wire in two_equal_bars_leaning_at_each_other.rs), are refused under all six fuses, where since Q1660 the same pair turned 50, 60, 70 or 100 degrees answers every one. As Q1660 left it, both unions are refused CannotNameWhichPieceOfACrossingThisIs, the intersections ACurvedFaceGoesRightRoundWithNoSeam and CannotMeshAFace CornersCoincide, and the differences CornersCoincide and AWireWillNotLieFlatOnItsFace. Measured by Q1660: grad S x grad T at the two points where the pipes touch is (1.6e-17, 0, 0) and not nought, as the points sit at y = +-6.4e-17, so the_corners_of_each_run_between_two_tangent_points in fuse/assemble.rs, which asks for exactly nought at both ends, does not keep the middle of each half ellipse, and the half folded from touch point to touch point cannot be named. Two roads named and not run: read which arc each edge either side of the middle is, since a Corner does not carry its arrange name, or choose the end where the surfaces cross at the wider angle. Close the gap, or demonstrate a limit by section 16.10 §31
